stateDiagram-v2
  [*] --> NOT_SCHEDULED: off-calendar (TEEP only; excluded from PPT)
  NOT_SCHEDULED --> RUNNING: shift starts, equipment producing
  RUNNING --> RUNNING: producing good/total counts
  RUNNING --> MINOR_STOP: short stop below micro-stop threshold (Performance / L3)
  MINOR_STOP --> RUNNING: auto-resume
  RUNNING --> BREAKDOWN: unplanned fault/trip above threshold (Availability / L1)
  BREAKDOWN --> RUNNING: repair done (M2 classifies failure mode/MTTR)
  RUNNING --> SETUP: planned changeover / roll change (Availability / L2)
  SETUP --> RUNNING: setup complete
  RUNNING --> PLANNED_STOP: break / no-demand / PM window (planned)
  PLANNED_STOP --> RUNNING: resume
  RUNNING --> NOT_SCHEDULED: shift ends

  note right of MINOR_STOP
    micro-stop threshold (60-120s) is the
    Availability / Performance seam (per work-unit)
  end note
  note right of BREAKDOWN
    one DowntimeEvent: M2 = failure view,
    M4 = Availability view (no double-count)
  end note
